Pin and build the fork point, boot it on the USG-3P, wire the bench, measure the stock baseline (G0), and run the hardware probes T0.5–T0.9 that Phase 2 depends on. Phase 0 includes both host builds and board work, and runs in parallel with Phase 1.

```
T0.1 pin ─ T0.2 build/boot ─ T0.3 bench ─ T0.4 baseline ─► [G0]
T0.5–T0.9 probes (any order after T0.2)
```

### Sub-issues

- T0.1 Pin the fork at c595b86dd344 and record file revisions {{T0.1}}
- T0.2 Build and boot loop: cross-build, TFTP boot, bsd.good recovery {{T0.2}}
- T0.3 Bench and artefacts: bench/ configs, traffic and capture scripts {{T0.3}}
- T0.4 Stock baseline measurements (G0) {{T0.4}}
- T0.5 Probe: PIP VLAN fields in WQE word2 {{T0.5}}
- T0.6 Probe: buffer data offsets and WQE LEN {{T0.6}}
- T0.7 Probe: RX groups and CPU mapping {{T0.7}}
- T0.8 Probe: FPA pool levels {{T0.8}}
- T0.9 Probe: interrupt yield mechanism (decides DESIGN §5.6 option A or B) {{T0.9}}
- G0 Gate: stock baseline recorded, go/no-go decided {{G0}}

Needs the OpenBSD build host ({{C2}}) and the board. T0.1's revision table and T0.3's bench files can be written at the desk.

