Acceptance gate from [SPEC §7.1]({{DOC:SPEC:7.1}}). Gates are hard stops: work that depends on this gate does not start until it is closed with evidence.

### Pass condition (SPEC §7.1, verbatim)

> All §7.2 functional, VLAN, invalidation, race, ordering, ARP, safety and 1-hour control-plane tests pass in mode 1; R13 measured. (Multi-day endurance soaks are verified in Phase 4 / T4.3). Decides whether Phase 3 (zero-copy) is worth starting.

### Decides

Mode 1 acceptance, and whether Phase 3 (zero-copy mode 2) is worth starting. R13 is a milestone, not a stopping point: record the remaining bottlenecks and the next useful optimization, or evidence that the workload is at its link limit.

### Evidence to attach before closing

- [ ] All SPEC §7.2 functional, VLAN, invalidation, race, ordering, ARP, safety and 1-hour control-plane tests pass in mode 1 ({{T2.6}}–{{T2.9}}).
- [ ] R13 measured per SPEC §7.3 and compared with G0; results in NOTES.md ({{T2.10}}).
- [ ] The Phase 3 decision and further mode-1 optimization work, as a comment here. Multi-day soaks are verified later in {{T4.3}} (ERRATA D15).

### Fed by

- T2.5 Mode 1 hit path: take, rewrite, batch, flush {{T2.5}}
- T2.6 Correctness and VLAN suites (mode 1) {{T2.6}}
- T2.7 Invalidation, static routing, OSPF and ARP suites (mode 1) {{T2.7}}
- T2.8 Safety suite (mode 1) {{T2.8}}
- T2.9 Control plane at full fast-path load (R12) {{T2.9}}
- T2.10 Measure mode 1 against G0 (R13), proves G3 {{T2.10}}

### Unblocks

Phase 3 (optional) and Phase 4.

