**As** the router owner, **I want** every relevant route, ARP, interface, VLAN, bridge/trunk, monitor, bpf, sysctl, pf or IPsec change to invalidate cached flows at admission, and the next hops of active flows to be refreshed in ARP, **so that** offloaded traffic never follows a stale forwarding decision beyond the documented queue tail.

### Requirement (SPEC §5, Must, verbatim)

> **R8** — Invalidation at admission per contract item 5, plus fair ARP refresh per item 6. Old-generation entries never pass a new admission check after the bump; queued packets are explicitly exempt.

